cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use blockyOS in your research, please cite it as below, including the version and the measurement protocol your results were produced with (recorded in every run's provenance)."
title: "blockyOS: a local lab for measuring how language models run on the hardware they're on"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: matco01
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-17
license: Apache-2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24324900
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24324900
    description: All versions (resolves to the latest)
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24324901
    description: Version 0.2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/matco01/blockyOS"
abstract: >-
  blockyOS is a self-hosted research environment for local language-model inference. It profiles complete
  configurations (weights, quantization, engine build, framework, context, device limits) with a fixed, versioned
  measurement protocol: paired accuracy tests on MMLU-Pro, KL divergence against a baseline's logits, repeated speed
  measurements with robust spread, energy per token, and a roofline-style hardware analysis. Every run records its
  provenance, comparisons refuse mismatched conditions, and instrument checks test that the measurement pipeline behaves
  correctly on the machine at hand.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - quantization
  - inference
  - benchmarking
  - reproducibility
  - llama.cpp
